  "purpose": "These three sequences separate the remaining plausible source behaviors: repeated same-key puts distinguish INSERT OR IGNORE from REPLACE/DO UPDATE and expose trigger effects; put-then-delete distinguishes direct change counts from trigger-inflated counts and from total_changes; cross-connection same-key puts distinguish main-only counters from main+other total_changes and expose conflict handling across connections."
